= main =
Thin end of the wedge type stuff. We can perceive dispositions such as
instability.

So playing fast and loose with the notion of perception. Is confusion
between thin and thick perception the key issue?

A hint of non-linguistic representation.
The assumption that since perception of XYZ is immediate/does not require
explicit inference, that therefore it is perceptual. The idea of non-linguisitc
theory is ommitted from consideration.
